What the assembly tells us
asmsub $0x50,%esp        ← allocates 0x50 = 80 bytes on stack
lea 0x10(%esp),%eax   ← buffer starts at esp+0x10 = 16 bytes offset
call gets             ← reads input with NO size limit ← vulnerable!
ret                   ← returns to... wherever return address points
So the actual buffer size is:
0x50 - 0x10 = 0x40 = 64 bytes

